---

## Objective

After B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It
documents foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product
implementation, approval, or release readiness.

## Context packet

Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,
`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,
`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and
`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.

## Output list

- `../runbooks/R0012.md` — IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.

## Required authoring content

Use standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:
B0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and
blank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,
required behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,
observable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is
needed and prohibiting incidental assets.

## Validation procedure

Stop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,
provenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every
required section and explicit retained gate.

## Checkpoint and update procedure

Update B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this
file on resume.

## Stop condition

Stop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.

## Acceptance criteria

- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.
- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.
- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.
- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.
