dency-policy manifest\"],\"api\":[\"Command, state, event, and adapter interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"concrete combat/exploration/UI\",\"account or network client\",\"target-specific campaign rules\"],\"verification\":\"A dependency-rule test rejects forbidden core imports and a fixture adapter proves command-only interaction.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"None; retain GATE-0001 for tool-specific enforcement.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"domain\":\"tests\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Layered unit, content, integration, and reserved browser-test conventions provide isolated RNG/clock and persistence fixtures with no real service or player data access.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"test-runner configuration\",\"tests/{core,content,platform,app}/fixtures\",\"docs/testing.md\"],\"data\":[\"deterministic fixture factories\"],\"api\":[\"test fixture and fake clock/RNG interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"final feature assertions\",\"real browser/device matrix claims\",\"production telemetry\"],\"verification\":\"Repeated core fixture execution has identical results; a deliberately failing fixture is detected; fixture storage is isolated.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 before compatibility or performance claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"domain\":\"data\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0010\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Immutable versioned state, command/result/event envelopes, revision and interaction identifiers, deterministic RNG state, and invariant helpers define legal transition mechanics without feature state machines.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/\",\"tests/core/contract.*\"],\"data\":[\"campaign snapshot envelope\",\"deterministic RNG state\"],\"api\":[\"Core command/state/event API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"authored values\",\"combat/inventory/quest algorithms\",\"save driver\",\"UI selection state\",\"account/network state\"],\"verification\":\"Invalid and stale commands do not mutate state; duplicate interaction IDs cause no extra durable transition.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 before concrete party/content shapes.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Typed content-package schema and validator cover IDs, references, locale keys, assets, predicates, rewards, and reachability but contain no authored campaign expression.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/\",\"tests/content/validation.*\",\"docs/content-authoring.md\"],\"data\":[\"versioned content package format\",\"asset/provenance manifest schema\"],\"api\":[\"content registry and validator API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"town/dungeon dialogue/maps/assets\",\"copied reference expression\",\"release packaging\"],\"verification\":\"Valid minimum package passes; each invalid reference class fails; a graph fixture checks opening-to-ending reachability.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 for quantities, locale, and content detail; human provenance review remains required.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A schema protocol specifies immutable revisions, checksums, current-pointer validation, known-good retention, quarantine, separate preferences, deletion confirmation, and safe-boundary persistence rules.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/\",\"src/platform/web/persistence/\",\"tests/{core,platform}/save*\",\"docs/save-and-recovery.md\"],\"data\":[\"save snapshot and preference schemas\",\"quarantine record\"],\"api\":[\"snapshot repository and recovery protocol\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"cloud sync\",\"identity\",\"PWA cache records\",\"eviction guarantee\"],\"verification\":\"Fault fixtures cover interrupted write, checksum failure, malformed data, quota/permission failure, quarantine, retry, and selected-slot deletion.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 storage API, quota, support window, and recovery policy.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Ordered, pure migrations declare supported versions and promote only validated candidates while preserving original invalid bytes for quarantine.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{migrations,compatibility}/\",\"tests/core/save/fixtures\"],\"data\":[\"migration registry and predecessor fixtures\"],\"api\":[\"migration runner API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"storage driver changes\",\"future data export\",\"automatic destructive repair\"],\"verification\":\"Every declared predecessor migrates once; unsupported or failed migration leaves the original candidate intact and quarantined.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 support-window approval.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0008\",\"title\":\"Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\",\"domain\":\"security\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0013\",\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Architecture and negative contract tests demonstrate that local campaign start/save/resume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, role, entitlement, multiplayer, or safety service.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/security-boundary.md\",\"tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*\"],\"data\":[\"future connected-service approval checklist\"],\"api\":[\"local-slot identity contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"sign-in\",\"OAuth\",\"sync\",\"roles\",\"moderation\",\"purchases\",\"server APIs\"],\"verification\":\"Static scan and negative fixtures find no identity/token/privilege fields or network client in P0 foundation modules.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 before any connected implementation.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0009\",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"domain\":\"privacy\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0006\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A bounded local diagnostic schema, consent and clear controls, redaction rules, and no-network guardrails support future player recovery without collecting save or dialogue payloads.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0006\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/platform/web/diagnostics/\",\"src/app/recovery/diagnostic-contract.*\",\"tests/platform/diagnostics.*\",\"docs/privacy-and-recovery.md\"],\"data\":[\"redacted local diagnostic record\",\"consent state\"],\"api\":[\"diagnostic recorder interface\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"diagnostic provider/transport\",\"remote analytics\",\"retention promise\",\"secrets\"],\"verification\":\"Tests prove diagnostics are absent without consent, redact payloads, and can be deleted locally.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 before transport, retention, hosting, or support claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"domain\":\"accessibility\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0010\",\"NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Original semantic tokens cover typography, spacing, focus, motion, touch targets, status, contrast, and non-colour cues, enabling later responsive web UI and inherited PWA UI.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/app/design/tokens/\",\"docs/design-tokens.md\",\"tests/app/design-tokens.*\"],\"data\":[\"semantic token inventory\"],\"api\":[\"token consumption contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"screens\",\"maps\",\"final artwork/fonts\",\"final breakpoints\",\"copied reference styling\"],\"verification\":\"Token validation proves semantic labels/non-colour cues and reduced-motion values in representative fixtures.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 before numeric contrast/font/breakpoint claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A provenance record format, review checklist, and source-asset manifest make authorship and permitted functional reference scope auditable before authored content enters a build.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"assets/source-manifest.*\",\"docs/original-content-review.md\",\"tests/content/provenance.*\"],\"data\":[\"provenance manifest and review disposition\"],\"api\":[\"provenance validator input contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"creating art/audio/story\",\"licensing approval\",\"automatic legal clearance\"],\"verification\":\"Validator rejects missing provenance fields; human creative review is recorded for each authored package.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"Human creative/provenance review; legal or licensing review if applicable under GATE-0007.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"domain\":\"documentation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0012\",\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Developer documentation records ownership, command flow, save-versus-cache separation, deferred connected scope, and the decisions/gates that later domain authors must preserve.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0008\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/{architecture,development,save-and-recovery,security-boundary}.md\"],\"data\":[\"foundation decision and ownership index\"],\"api\":[\"documented public-boundary inventory\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"player release guide\",\"operational rollout\",\"claiming approved vendor or policy choices\"],\"verification\":\"Documentation review cross-checks every foundation contract's ownership, dependency, and gate against this catalogue.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"None; approval gates are documented, not resolved.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"}\n  ],\n  \"expansion_queue\": [\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"exploration\",\"dialogue\",\"quests\",\"tutorial\",\"combat\",\"inventory\",\"party progression\",\"town/dungeon/ending content\",\"content validation\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared core and content only; no UI ownership\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-03\",\"title\":\"Session, UI, input, and accessibility\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\"],\"covers\":[\"session/checkpoints\",\"semantic responsive shell\",\"game panels\",\"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad adapters\",\"settings\",\"localisation\",\"captions\",\"feedback\",\"error recovery UI\",\"accessibility tests\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0009\",\"REQ-0010\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0003,GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared UI model; web input/layout adapter; PWA inherits UI with no separate UI fork\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-04\",\"title\":\"PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\"],\"covers\":[\"PWA manifest/install\",\"service-worker cache lifecycle\",\"offline/update recovery\",\"performance measurement\",\"security headers\",\"release checks\",\"observability\",\"quality automation\",\"player/operator documentation\",\"platform certification assessment\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0011\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0001\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0006\",\"NFR-0009\",\"NFR-0011\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0005,GATE-0007\",\"target_allocation\":\"web release build and PWA service-worker/install adapter are distinct; shared core owns neither cache nor hosting\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-05\",\"title\":\"Connected-scope decision package\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"identity/sync conflict policy\",\"multiplayer/player safety\",\"live operations\",\"commerce/entitlements\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0006\",\"target_allocation\":\"no P0 target implementation; research/decision outputs only if explicitly authorised\",\"state\":\"hold\"}\n  ],\n  \"requirement_coverage\": {\n    \"REQ-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-02; provenance foundation IMP-0011\",\"REQ-0002\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0003\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0004\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0005\":\"queued: SHARD-02 and SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0007\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0009\":\"queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0010\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0011\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0013\":\"current: IMP-0002, IMP-0008\",\"REQ-0014\":\"gated: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"REQ-0015\":\"hold: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"NFR-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0002\":\"current/gated: IMP-0004, IMP-0006, IMP-0007\",\"NFR-0003\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0004\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0005\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0007\":\"current: IMP-0005; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0010, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0009\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0002\",\"NFR-0010\":\"current: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004; queued target adapters in SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0011\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0005\",\"NFR-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0008, IMP-0012; queued: SHARD-04\"\n  },\n  \"dependency_graph\": {\"nodes\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\"],\"acyclic\":true,\"validation\":\"Each prerequisite points only to an earlier numbered contract; SHARD dependencies only point from later shards to earlier shards.\"}\n}\n---\ntask_id: F014\nsequence: 14\ntitle: Generate the bounded implementation-runbook authoring collection\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nGenerate only the bootstrap wave of ordinary Supervisor runbooks in\n`projects/<project-slug>/authoring-runbooks/`: a bounded catalogue-expansion\ntask followed by a dispatcher task. The dispatcher allocates at most ten\nauthoring B-series tasks per wave, creates one successor dispatcher, and stops.\nEach authoring task instructs Codex to create only its assigned R-series\nimplementation runbooks under\n`projects/<project-slug>/runbooks/`, then validate their metadata and update the\nmanifest. The successor dispatcher repeats this process until no queued\ncatalogue chapter or unassigned implementation contract remains. Generate an\n`INITIAL.md` context document in `authoring-runbooks/`\nthat points to the canonical `PROJECT_BRIEF.md` and specification.\n\nRegister the generated authoring collection with the source collection by\nwriting `runbooks/.supervisor-children/<project-slug>.json` containing\n`{\"runbooks_dir\": \"../projects/<project-slug>/authoring-runbooks\"}`. Also\nwrite `authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json` containing\n`{\"runbooks_dir\": \"../runbooks\"}`. These are explicit child-collection\nregistrations; `supervisor-run --run-all` follows them automatically after the\nparent collection is accepted.\n\nEvery dispatcher first expands at most one queued specification/catalogue domain\nchapter (maximum 250 `IMP-*` contracts), validates its coverage, then allocates\nready contracts. If any queued chapter or ready contract remains, it creates no\nmore than ten authoring tasks and exactly one successor dispatcher. If none\nremains, it creates the final audit task instead. This is a durable loop, not a\nrecursive prompt or an unbounded single run.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must use the standard Supervisor front matter\nand contain: precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs; owned\nfiles/data/interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; platform differences;\nverification commands/evidence; and observable acceptance criteria. It must be\nsmall enough for one implementation task, not a vague epic.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must retain machine-readable provenance to the\ncanonical decisions that justify it. Its front matter must declare all of these\nnon-empty fields, using comma-separated values where more than one applies:\n\n```yaml\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#save-state\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-SAVE-001\nauthoring_batch: B0007\nfactory_stages: F003,F005,F012,F013\n```\n\n`source_specifications` points to the smallest relevant canonical\nspecification section; `source_catalogue_ids` identifies the allocated\nimplementation-catalogue records; `authoring_batch` identifies the B-series\nwriter that created the R file; and `factory_stages` identifies the F-series\nstages that established the requirement. This is a traceability trail, not an\ninstruction to inject every F or B runbook into the implementation agent's\nprompt. The R task uses these links to read only the canonical context it needs.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must also include a detailed asset assessment.\nIts front matter must always declare both fields below, even when no assets are\nneeded:\n\n```yaml\nasset_impact: required # or not_applicable\nasset_ids: village_gate_main,village_gate_construction # blank only when not_applicable\n```\n\nFor `asset_impact: required`, the B-series writer must reserve stable,\nproduct-specific asset IDs (never generic names such as `image1`), provide an\n`asset_brief` and `visual_style_version`, and include an `## Asset assessment`\nsection explaining the assets' purpose, where they appear, the required visual\nstates/variants, source-of-truth ownership, and original-art acceptance checks.\nFor `not_applicable`, that section must explain why the scope needs no generated\nor source visual asset and explicitly prohibit incidental asset creation. This\nkeeps UI, illustration, icon, texture, sprite, audio-visual, and other product\nasset work visible in the implementation plan instead of discovering it midway\nthrough coding.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must also declare an audio assessment, even\nwhen audio is not needed:\n\n```yaml\naudio_impact: required # or not_applicable\naudio_ids: ember_menu_loop # blank only when not_applicable\naudio_brief: 30-second seamless instrumental menu cue # blank only when not_applicable\naudio_duration_seconds: 30 # 0 only when not_applicable\naudio_loop: required # required, not_required, or not_applicable\naudio_style_version: project-audio-v1\n```\n\nFor `audio_impact: required`, the writer must reserve stable cue IDs, cite the\nrelevant `04-audio-direction.md` section, describe the in-product trigger and\nmix/accessibility expectations, and assign a sensible duration and loop policy.\nThe Supervisor's separate local audio lane then creates a manifest, invokes\nACE-Step, and performs technical/provenance QA before coding begins. For\n`not_applicable`, every audio field has the stated empty/default form so an\notherwise unrelated task cannot silently generate music or sound effects.\n\nEach B-series authoring task may create at most seven R-series implementation\nrunbooks. It must stop after its assigned seven (or fewer), update the manifest,\nand leave remaining work for the next bounded batch.\n\nAn unresolved framework, legal, service, design, or other human gate is never\npermission for a B-series writer to omit its assigned R files or wait for an\nearlier B batch to be accepted. The writer produces the bounded contract now,\nrecords the gate and any R-to-R implementation dependency explicitly, and lets\nthe later R-series product-work run pause at that genuine decision. In short:\n**gates block implementation, not runbook authoring**.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The initial collection contains only a bounded bootstrap wave; each\n  dispatcher expands at most one 250-contract domain shard, creates at most ten\n  new B-series authoring tasks plus one successor, then exits. It never attempts\n  to materialise the whole game plan.\n- There is exactly one valid B-series authoring runbook per allocated manifest\n  batch, and it creates no more than seven assigned R-series runbooks.\n- B-series runbooks never overwrite an existing R-series contract with a\n  conflicting ID; they stop and report mismatches.\n- Every generated B-series runbook includes its context packet, output list,\n  validation procedure, checkpoint/update procedure, and a clear stop condition.\n- Every generated B-series runbook states that it must author its allocated R\n  files despite unresolved implementation gates or unimplemented R\n  dependencies, retaining those gates in the R contract rather than stopping.\n- Both child-collection registration files exist, contain valid JSON with a\n  relative `runbooks_dir`, and point to the generated authoring and\n  implementation collections respectively.\n- R-series contracts use stable IDs and parse with the Supervisor runbook\n  loader; their declared dependencies match the manifest, every contract has\n  explicit `asset_impact` and `asset_ids` metadata, and asset-required\n  contracts have non-empty stable IDs. Every R contract also has non-empty,\n  valid `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`,\n  and `factory_stages` provenance metadata.\n- Every R-series contract has explicit valid audio metadata. Audio-required\n  contracts have stable IDs, a non-empty cue brief, duration, loop policy,\n  audio-style version, and a source link to the canonical audio direction.\n- The collection contains a final audit B-series task after all authoring\n  batches and catalogue expansions are complete, rather than pretending that\n  thousands of contracts can be reviewed in one generation step.\n---\ntask_id: B0006\nsequence: 7\ntitle: Author the foundation documentation closure contract\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nAfter B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It\ndocuments foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product\nimplementation, approval, or release readiness.\n\n## Context packet\n\nRead `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,\n`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and\n`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `../runbooks/R0012.md` \u2014 IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.\n\n## Required authoring content\n\nUse standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:\nB0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\nblank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,\nrequired behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,\nobservable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is\nneeded and prohibiting incidental assets.\n\n## Validation procedure\n\nStop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,\nprovenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every\nrequired section and explicit retained gate.\n\n## Checkpoint and update procedure\n\nUpdate B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this\nfile on resume.\n\n## Stop condition\n\nStop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.\n- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.\n- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.\n- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.\nsed: projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-ledger.md: No such file or directory\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/decision-log.md:10:| DEC-0004 | Party/content quantities, balance, locale, audio/remapping, font/contrast / game+experience owner / before DM-04/16 | approved production choices | one bounded campaign only; no numeric/content promise | GATE-0004 |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:22:src/core/                 deterministic, browser-free rules and state\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:37:| DM-02 | Define immutable domain state, typed commands/results/events, revisions, interaction IDs, deterministic RNG state, and invariant helpers with no browser imports. | DM-01 | `src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}`; `tests/core/contract.*` | Unit tests prove command rejection is non-mutating and expected-revision checks reject stale requests. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:48:| DM-08 | Implement quest, dialogue, campaign, and tutorial state machines, including idempotent objective/reward/checkpoint ordering and ending completion. | DM-02, DM-03, DM-04, DM-05 | `src/core/{quest,dialogue,campaign,tutorial}`; `tests/core/campaign.*` | Tests cover repeated interaction, locked predicates, one-time rewards, tutorial progression, and ending transition. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:51:| DM-11 | Implement scene exploration rules for collision, interactions, exits, encounter zones, and safe scene boundaries across exactly one town and one dungeon. | DM-02, DM-03, DM-04, DM-08, DM-09 | `src/core/exploration/`; `tests/core/exploration.*` | Scripted route traverses town to dungeon to ending; locked exit and missing/invalid content states fail safely. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:58:| DM-13 | Build the responsive semantic application shell: title/new/continue/load navigation, pause/focus/visibility behaviour, game stage, panels, status messages, and error-boundary entry points. | DM-01, DM-07, DM-12 | `src/app/{shell,navigation,status}`; `tests/app/shell.*`; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/dm-13-shell-navigation.spec.*` | App integration tests; Playwright covers no-save title state, panel return target, focus-loss pause, and phone/tablet/desktop shell reflow. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:59:| DM-14 | Deliver exploration, dialogue, quest, party, inventory, combat, and ending presentation bound only to core state/events, with readable empty/locked/invalid feedback. | DM-04, DM-08\u2013DM-13 | `src/app/{game,panels,combat,dialogue}`; `tests/app/gameplay-ui.*`; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/dm-14-gameplay-ui.spec.*` | State-driven UI tests; Playwright completes the tutorial battle and verifies empty inventory, locked exit, visible objective, and ending path. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:67:| DM-17 | Add PWA manifest, install affordance, asset manifest/precache, offline status, known-good cache retention, and safe-boundary update activation independent from saves. | DM-04\u2013DM-07, DM-12\u2013DM-16; service-worker rollout approval | `public/{manifest,icons}`; `src/platform/web/pwa/`; service-worker/build config; `tests/platform/pwa.*`; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/dm-17-pwa-lifecycle.spec.*` | Browser test covers uncached offline explanation, cached offline reload, declined/unavailable install, refresh failure retention, and update deferred until title/pause after confirmed save. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:70:| DM-20 | Produce player and operator release material: controls/help, save/recovery and privacy guidance, accessibility statement, support/version/cache status, content authoring/release checklist, rollback procedure, and release compatibility declaration. | DM-04\u2013DM-19 | `docs/{player-guide,accessibility,privacy-and-recovery,release-runbook,rollback,content-authoring}.md`; in-app Help/Status copy | Documentation review against contracts; dry-run release/rollback using a known-good build without changing player saves. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:30:| J3 | Explore and advance the campaign: player finishes town, dungeon, and ending. | Talk to characters \u2192 accept quest \u2192 traverse town/dungeon \u2192 resolve required encounter and objective \u2192 claim reward \u2192 see ending. | Locked exits state the missing quest condition; exhausted dialogue has a safe closing line; missing authored reference fails content validation and shows recoverable error rather than breaking state; optional reward absence never blocks completion. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:31:| J4 | Manage items and progression: player can use earned resources correctly. | Open inventory \u2192 inspect item \u2192 use/equip only where legal \u2192 see immediate feedback \u2192 close back to play. | Empty inventory has an explicit empty state; invalid use, full/limited capacity (if authored), or ineligible target preserves inventory; quest items cannot be discarded if that would make a required path impossible. Deletion/discard is not a first-release capability unless an authored safe rule is later approved. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:32:| J5 | Save, load, and recover: player can leave and return safely. | Manual save or checkpoint completes atomically \u2192 resume chooses latest valid save \u2192 state restores at a safe scene boundary. | No save slot shows explanation; corrupt/incompatible candidate is quarantined, never overwritten, and falls back to the last valid checkpoint or new game; storage denial/quota exposes retry and export/support guidance where feasible; interrupted write keeps prior confirmed save. Local cache and any future remote copy conflict resolve only with explicit player choice; remote sync is not first release. Deleting a save requires confirmation and removes only that selected local save. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:34:| J7 | Install, update, and recover from a fault: player retains a coherent playable version. | Install when browser allows \u2192 cache approved release \u2192 play offline \u2192 accept update at launch/menu after save boundary. | Installation prompt may be unavailable/declined without blocking web play; offline uncached assets state the requirement; cache refresh failure retains known-good cache; crash/error boundary offers retry, return to title, and safe recovery. Diagnostics are minimal and consent-gated where required; a player can decline or delete local diagnostic data without losing play. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:36:## Domain vocabulary and state ownership\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:40:| Campaign | The fixed first-release sequence from new game through ending; owns completion state. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:42:| Quest | Authored objective and state machine that gates campaign progress and rewards. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:46:| Save snapshot | Versioned, validated, atomic representation of durable player state at a safe boundary. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:47:| Checkpoint | Authored or system-selected safe snapshot point; it is not a promise to restore arbitrary moment-to-moment state. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:72:- An encounter may read party, item, and quest state but changes durable state\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:84:- The local offline campaign neither needs identity nor sends player state.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:95:combat advancement; focus loss pauses or reaches a safe state; UI action labels\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:150:states; `RewardGrant` is `unclaimed \u2192 applied`. Inputs are item definitions,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:165:campaign/quest/party/inventory/settings state, checkpoint triggers, and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:179:is emitted by action/scene/combat state. Inputs are accessible labels, text\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md:226:| P0 | Dialogue, quest state, onboarding, short ending | Understand and complete story progress (J1\u2013J3). | First release |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md:28:| ID | Domain | Outcome | Prerequisites | Gate/status |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md:33:| IMP-0004 | Data | Deterministic state/command/event contract | IMP-0002\u20130003 | current |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md:45:scope, verification, human/external gate, complexity, and status. The only\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md:53:| SHARD-02 | Campaign content and domain logic (250) | SHARD-01 | Core P0 campaign; GATE-0004 | Shared core/content; no UI |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/domain-completeness-review.md:12:| Persistence/recovery | SPEC-02/03; snapshot/checkpoint; atomic/version/quarantine rules | all durable game state, PWA cache | schema/migrations/fixtures | P0, storage policy gated |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validation-report.md:16:  \"state\": \"ready_for_authoring\"\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validation-report.md:37:Chapter states verified:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validation-report.md:38:- SHARD-02: queued (depends on SHARD-01)\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validation-report.md:39:- SHARD-03: queued (depends on SHARD-01, SHARD-02)\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validation-report.md:40:- SHARD-04: queued (depends on SHARD-01, SHARD-02, SHARD-03)\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validation-report.md:47:No R-series implementation runbook files exist outside of .state. The stray `runbooks/R0001.md` was removed as it violated the validation checkpoint (B0001 should be authoring before producing R0001, not pre-created).\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validation-report.md:67:- Future shard expansion (SHARD-02 through SHARD-05) blocked pending gate approvals\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md:19:| Game shell and responsive renderer | J1, J3, J6; readable mobile-to-desktop play | Owns navigation, focus/visibility pause, semantic UI, visual settings, and rendering only. It requests domain commands and renders returned state/events. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md:20:| Input adapters | Keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad accessibility | Convert platform events into a shared, remappable `InputAction` vocabulary; unavailable hardware is non-fatal. No adapter may mutate campaign state directly. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md:21:| Deterministic rules core | Tutorial combat, quests, inventory, progression | Owns legal state transitions, seeded/randomness policy, combat resolution, reward ledger, and invariants. Command validation precedes every mutation. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md:27:### Dependency direction and state rules\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md:32:web/PWA shell + renderer <\u2500\u2500 state/events \u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500> save/recovery repository\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md:37:Only the rules core can produce durable campaign state. The shell owns\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-t