,\"account/network state\"],\"verification\":\"Invalid and stale commands do not mutate state; duplicate interaction IDs cause no extra durable transition.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 before concrete party/content shapes.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:12:    {\"id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Typed content-package schema and validator cover IDs, references, locale keys, assets, predicates, rewards, and reachability but contain no authored campaign expression.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/\",\"tests/content/validation.*\",\"docs/content-authoring.md\"],\"data\":[\"versioned content package format\",\"asset/provenance manifest schema\"],\"api\":[\"content registry and validator API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"town/dungeon dialogue/maps/assets\",\"copied reference expression\",\"release packaging\"],\"verification\":\"Valid minimum package passes; each invalid reference class fails; a graph fixture checks opening-to-ending reachability.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 for quantities, locale, and content detail; human provenance review remains required.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:13:    {\"id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A schema protocol specifies immutable revisions, checksums, current-pointer validation, known-good retention, quarantine, separate preferences, deletion confirmation, and safe-boundary persistence rules.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/\",\"src/platform/web/persistence/\",\"tests/{core,platform}/save*\",\"docs/save-and-recovery.md\"],\"data\":[\"save snapshot and preference schemas\",\"quarantine record\"],\"api\":[\"snapshot repository and recovery protocol\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"cloud sync\",\"identity\",\"PWA cache records\",\"eviction guarantee\"],\"verification\":\"Fault fixtures cover interrupted write, checksum failure, malformed data, quota/permission failure, quarantine, retry, and selected-slot deletion.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 storage API, quota, support window, and recovery policy.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:14:    {\"id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Ordered, pure migrations declare supported versions and promote only validated candidates while preserving original invalid bytes for quarantine.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{migrations,compatibility}/\",\"tests/core/save/fixtures\"],\"data\":[\"migration registry and predecessor fixtures\"],\"api\":[\"migration runner API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"storage driver changes\",\"future data export\",\"automatic destructive repair\"],\"verification\":\"Every declared predecessor migrates once; unsupported or failed migration leaves the original candidate intact and quarantined.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 support-window approval.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:15:    {\"id\":\"IMP-0008\",\"title\":\"Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\",\"domain\":\"security\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0013\",\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Architecture and negative contract tests demonstrate that local campaign start/save/resume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, role, entitlement, multiplayer, or safety service.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/security-boundary.md\",\"tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*\"],\"data\":[\"future connected-service approval checklist\"],\"api\":[\"local-slot identity contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"sign-in\",\"OAuth\",\"sync\",\"roles\",\"moderation\",\"purchases\",\"server APIs\"],\"verification\":\"Static scan and negative fixtures find no identity/token/privilege fields or network client in P0 foundation modules.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 before any connected implementation.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:16:    {\"id\":\"IMP-0009\",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"domain\":\"privacy\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0006\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A bounded local diagnostic schema, consent and clear controls, redaction rules, and no-network guardrails support future player recovery without collecting save or dialogue payloads.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0006\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/platform/web/diagnostics/\",\"src/app/recovery/diagnostic-contract.*\",\"tests/platform/diagnostics.*\",\"docs/privacy-and-recovery.md\"],\"data\":[\"redacted local diagnostic record\",\"consent state\"],\"api\":[\"diagnostic recorder interface\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"diagnostic provider/transport\",\"remote analytics\",\"retention promise\",\"secrets\"],\"verification\":\"Tests prove diagnostics are absent without consent, redact payloads, and can be deleted locally.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 before transport, retention, hosting, or support claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:17:    {\"id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"domain\":\"accessibility\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0010\",\"NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Original semantic tokens cover typography, spacing, focus, motion, touch targets, status, contrast, and non-colour cues, enabling later responsive web UI and inherited PWA UI.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/app/design/tokens/\",\"docs/design-tokens.md\",\"tests/app/design-tokens.*\"],\"data\":[\"semantic token inventory\"],\"api\":[\"token consumption contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"screens\",\"maps\",\"final artwork/fonts\",\"final breakpoints\",\"copied reference styling\"],\"verification\":\"Token validation proves semantic labels/non-colour cues and reduced-motion values in representative fixtures.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 before numeric contrast/font/breakpoint claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:18:    {\"id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A provenance record format, review checklist, and source-asset manifest make authorship and permitted functional reference scope auditable before authored content enters a build.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"assets/source-manifest.*\",\"docs/original-content-review.md\",\"tests/content/provenance.*\"],\"data\":[\"provenance manifest and review disposition\"],\"api\":[\"provenance validator input contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"creating art/audio/story\",\"licensing approval\",\"automatic legal clearance\"],\"verification\":\"Validator rejects missing provenance fields; human creative review is recorded for each authored package.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"Human creative/provenance review; legal or licensing review if applicable under GATE-0007.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:19:    {\"id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"domain\":\"documentation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0012\",\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Developer documentation records ownership, command flow, save-versus-cache separation, deferred connected scope, and the decisions/gates that later domain authors must preserve.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0008\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/{architecture,development,save-and-recovery,security-boundary}.md\"],\"data\":[\"foundation decision and ownership index\"],\"api\":[\"documented public-boundary inventory\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"player release guide\",\"operational rollout\",\"claiming approved vendor or policy choices\"],\"verification\":\"Documentation review cross-checks every foundation contract's ownership, dependency, and gate against this catalogue.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"None; approval gates are documented, not resolved.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"}\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:22:    {\"id\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"exploration\",\"dialogue\",\"quests\",\"tutorial\",\"combat\",\"inventory\",\"party progression\",\"town/dungeon/ending content\",\"content validation\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared core and content only; no UI ownership\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:23:    {\"id\":\"SHARD-03\",\"title\":\"Session, UI, input, and accessibility\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\"],\"covers\":[\"session/checkpoints\",\"semantic responsive shell\",\"game panels\",\"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad adapters\",\"settings\",\"localisation\",\"captions\",\"feedback\",\"error recovery UI\",\"accessibility tests\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0009\",\"REQ-0010\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0003,GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared UI model; web input/layout adapter; PWA inherits UI with no separate UI fork\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:24:    {\"id\":\"SHARD-04\",\"title\":\"PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\"],\"covers\":[\"PWA manifest/install\",\"service-worker cache lifecycle\",\"offline/update recovery\",\"performance measurement\",\"security headers\",\"release checks\",\"observability\",\"quality automation\",\"player/operator documentation\",\"platform certification assessment\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0011\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0001\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0006\",\"NFR-0009\",\"NFR-0011\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0005,GATE-0007\",\"target_allocation\":\"web release build and PWA service-worker/install adapter are distinct; shared core owns neither cache nor hosting\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:25:    {\"id\":\"SHARD-05\",\"title\":\"Connected-scope decision package\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"identity/sync conflict policy\",\"multiplayer/player safety\",\"live operations\",\"commerce/entitlements\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0006\",\"target_allocation\":\"no P0 target implementation; research/decision outputs only if explicitly authorised\",\"state\":\"hold\"}\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:28:    \"REQ-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-02; provenance foundation IMP-0011\",\"REQ-0002\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0003\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0004\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0005\":\"queued: SHARD-02 and SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0007\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0009\":\"queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0010\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0011\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0013\":\"current: IMP-0002, IMP-0008\",\"REQ-0014\":\"gated: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"REQ-0015\":\"hold: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"NFR-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0002\":\"current/gated: IMP-0004, IMP-0006, IMP-0007\",\"NFR-0003\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0004\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0005\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0007\":\"current: IMP-0005; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0010, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0009\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0002\",\"NFR-0010\":\"current: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004; queued target adapters in SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0011\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0005\",\"NFR-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0008, IMP-0012; queued: SHARD-04\"\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/00-domain-discovery.md:17:| Quest state, progression, rewards, and onboarding/tutorial | explicit | Quests, progression, and onboarding are required; first session teaches battle and saving. | Required capabilities; first useful session |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/00-domain-discovery.md:31:| Account identity, authentication, remote state sync, and conflict handling | requires-decision | Named as required but no account/sync policy exists and it conflicts with offline scope. | Required capabilities; cross-platform data policy |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/00-domain-discovery.md:33:| Live-service operations, status, support, incident response, and event tooling | requires-decision | Named as required but conflicts with a deliberately small offline release. | Required capabilities; creation scope |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/00-domain-discovery.md:51:they require explicit degraded states, privacy/security rules, operational\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:15:Every browser record owns its stated Playwright path and must provide both the\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:34:- **Invariants / validation:** Scene IDs, exits, interaction targets, and predicates must resolve in validated content. Movement cannot cross collision or a locked exit; a locked route names its unmet requirement. Invalid/missing content fails safely without corrupting campaign state.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:36:- **Responsive / accessibility:** Keyboard, touch, mouse, and detected gamepad invoke the same move/interact actions. Canvas/world interaction has adjacent labelled action routes and textual state; no required route depends on hover, drag, or tiny targets.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:41:- **Target / ownership:** Shared narrative state and panels; `src/core/{dialogue,quest,campaign}` and `src/app/{dialogue,panels}`; browser evidence `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/fex-03-quest-ending.spec.*`.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:42:- **Player-visible behaviour:** Dialogue shows speaker, a short readable turn, and explicit continue/response choices. Quest UI states what happened, next action, and destination. Objective updates are visible near the objective and in the quest panel. Completing the beacon sequence returns the player to town, marks the campaign complete, and presents the short ending.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:43:- **Invariants / validation:** Locked dialogue/quest predicates do not mutate state; an interaction ID can complete an objective or grant a reward once only. Ending cannot trigger before its authored predicates and cannot duplicate completion on reload.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:44:- **Persistence /recovery:** Quest and ending state are saved only after a complete transition; a crash or failed save resumes the last confirmed objective/checkpoint. Current dialogue is never included in diagnostics.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:51:- **Player-visible behaviour:** Combat announces the active turn, exposes only legal actions, requires an explicit target where needed, displays the outcome, and returns to the next decision. Illegal/unavailable choices state why without consuming a turn. Victory gives the authored reward once. Defeat offers recovery at the prior confirmed checkpoint.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:52:- **Invariants / validation:** Commands require current revision and legal actor/action/target; stale, repeated, or invalid commands are non-mutating and do not advance RNG or turn state. Encounter resolution and reward ledgers are deterministic for a fixture seed.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:60:- **Player-visible behaviour:** Bag and Party panels show item/character names, usable eligibility, effects, and clear empty state. Players may inspect and use/equip valid items on valid targets. Quest items are visibly protected. Rewards visibly confirm acquisition.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:61:- **Invariants / validation:** Item IDs, effects, target eligibility, capacity/equipment rules, and reward ledger are content-validated. Invalid use, ineligible target, protected quest-item removal, and duplicate reward grant leave state unchanged and explain the reason.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:70:- **Target / ownership:** Web shell; `src/app/{shell,navigation,status}`; browser evidence `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/fex-06-shell-navigation.spec.*`.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:71:- **Player-visible behaviour:** The primary game workspace has landmarked title/navigation, main controls, objective/status, and temporary titled panels. Pause is available via visible control, Escape, and mapped gamepad action at safe playable states. Focus loss/hidden tab pauses once per session with an explanation.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:73:- **Responsive:** Phone uses safe-area-aware world view, compact objective, reachable bottom controls and full-screen panels; tablet uses contextual side/bottom panels; desktop uses a collapsible status rail. Resize, rotation, zoom, virtual keyboard, and display-mode changes preserve state/selection or move focus to the panel heading with a status message.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:74:- **Acceptance evidence:** App navigation/focus tests; Playwright covers no-save title state, return target, focus-loss pause, Back behaviour, and phone/tablet/desktop reflow.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:88:- **Invariants / validation:** Focus indicator is at least 3 CSS px and 3:1 against adjacent colours; essential text is 4.5:1, targets are 44 CSS px minimum, and 200% text has no clipped/lost action or horizontal page scroll. Essential state always has text and non-colour cues. Reset describes affected preferences, confirms, and never alters campaign state.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:92:### FEX-09 \u2014 Audio, visual, and status feedback\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:94:- **Target / ownership:** Shared feedback semantics; `src/app/{status,feedback,design}` and content manifests; browser evidence `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/fex-09-feedback.spec.*`.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:95:- **Player-visible behaviour:** Victory, item gained, blocked route, invalid action, save result, update readiness, and recovery use concise text plus icon/shape, optional supported audio/haptic feedback, and non-blocking visual change. Status history remains reviewable in the objective/status panel.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:98:- **Acceptance evidence:** Status deduplication/review tests, non-colour semantic-state fixture, reduced-motion fixture, and Playwright verifies that blocked, save, recovery, and reward feedback retain a text/non-colour meaning with captions or reduced motion enabled.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:105:- **Player-visible behaviour:** Save data exposes valid slots, load, selected-slot deletion, recovery status, and clear explanations for no saves, corrupt saves, interrupted writes, quota/permission failures, and unsupported saves. Save success is stated only after confirmation.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:113:- **Player-visible behaviour:** An unexpected fault shows plain-language `Retry`, `Return to title`, and `Safe recovery` actions. Recovery is separate from optional diagnostics; clear diagnostics states its local-only effect.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:116:- **Acceptance evidence:** Recovery state-machine and redaction/consent/clear tests; Playwright injected-fault flow verifies all recovery paths and no diagnostics before consent.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:120:- **Target / ownership:** PWA adapter/status; `src/platform/web/pwa`, `public/{manifest,icons}`, service-worker config; browser evidence `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/fex-12-pwa-lifecycle.spec.*`.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:121:- **Player-visible behaviour:** Installation is optional and its unavailable/declined state is non-blocking. An uncached first offline visit explains that assets must download before play; a known-good cached version remains playable offline. PWA status distinguishes asset/cache state from save data.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:132:- **Invariants / validation:** Package version, IDs, references, localisation keys, assets, predicates, rewards, and reachability validate before release. The opening-to-ending graph must be reachable; invalid/missing asset or reference fixtures fail without shipping. Provenance records identify original creation/source status.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:139:- **Player-visible behaviour:** Help explains controls, save/recovery, accessibility, privacy, version/cache status, and support paths. Release copy makes no promise beyond approved browser/device, performance, localisation, or assistive-technology decisions.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:21:\u251c\u2500\u2500 Save data \u2192 load, delete-confirmation, recovery status\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:23:\u2514\u2500\u2500 PWA status \u2192 install guidance, offline readiness, safe update state\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:33:- `Escape`, a visible pause affordance, and the mapped gamepad pause action open pause at any safe playable state. Focus loss or tab hiding pauses the game and explains this only once per session.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:35:- Modal layers are reserved for blocking choices: save deletion, settings reset, a new-game replacement of an existing active slot, and a recovery choice. They state consequence, affected slot/data, irreversible status, and a safe default (`Cancel`). No timed dialog expires.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:53:| `--text-primary`, `--text-muted` | Primary is used for all essential content. Muted text is never the only carrier of an instruction, state, or warning and meets 4.5:1 when conveying necessary text. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:54:| `--accent-action`, `--state-success/warning/danger` | Accent is paired with text and a distinct icon/shape. Focus does not rely on the action colour. Error and destructive states use wording plus iconography. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:64:| Desktop / wide | Centred game stage with persistent but collapsible objective/status rail. Inventory and quest can use a two-column inspection layout; combat keeps actions and party/enemy status simultaneously visible. Mouse hover may preview a definition but never supplies essential information. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:66:Rotation, resize, zoom, virtual keyboards, and PWA display-mode changes preserve the current game state and selection where practical. If reflow temporarily obscures the selected control, focus moves to the panel heading and a short status message announces the layout change. Full screen is optional and provides an obvious exit path.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:77:| Gamepad | Feature-detect rather than promise a model. Show button glyphs only after detection and accompany them with action text. D-pad/left stick navigates; primary face button confirms; secondary face button cancels; menu button pauses; shoulder buttons may switch top-level panels when discoverable. A disconnected controller preserves state and presents keyboard/mouse/touch alternatives without blocking. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:79:| Voice and other assistive input | Voice command recognition is not collected, enabled, or required in P0. Controls expose standard semantic HTML roles, names, states, and operable buttons so browser voice control, switch control, eye tracking, and other assistive input can target visible actions by label. Canvas/world interactions have equivalent labelled UI prompts and action-list routes. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:85:- Use semantic landmarks for banner/title navigation, main game controls, complementary objective/status, and dialogs. Mark decorative art as hidden from assistive technology. Give the world canvas a concise labelled description and provide its essential current state through adjacent semantic status and action elements.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:87:- Dialogues announce speaker and text through a controlled, non-interrupting status mechanism; combat announces turn start, selected action/target, damage/healing, and victory/defeat without flooding announcements for decorative animation frames. Notifications are concise, deduplicated, and reviewable in the status/quest panel.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:89:- Do not use flicker above three flashes per second. Provide captions/subtitles for all non-text audio that conveys story, instruction, combat state, or warning; identify speaker and relevant sound in concise text. Master audio, music, effects, caption visibility, text size, contrast, and motion settings are reachable before starting a new game and while paused.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:90:- Required state has a text equivalent: party health uses values and state wording as well as bars; enemy intent uses a label/icon; map interaction, quest progression, and save status use text. Visual settings include a higher-contrast mode and non-colour state markers.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:92:- Settings save independently of campaign saves where storage permits. If persistence fails, keep the in-session choice, state that it will not persist, and preserve a usable default. Reset settings is confirmed and describes the affected preference categories.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:94:## Empty, error, recovery, destructive, and privacy-sensitive states\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:99:| Invalid action, locked exit, unavailable target | Keep the player\u2019s state and turn intact; name the unmet requirement and return focus to the legal choices. Do not use a generic `Error` as the only explanation. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:101:| Offline, install, cache, or update state | Explain whether the current cached version can play, whether an initial download is required, and that an update will wait for a save-safe title/menu boundary. Declining install or update does not block play on a valid cached/current release. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:104:| New game over an active slot / reset settings | Explain precisely what will change. New game must use a separate slot or obtain explicit confirmation before replacing a selected slot. Settings reset affects preferences only, not campaign state. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:105:| Diagnostics and local data | P0 sends no telemetry. Before any consent-gated local diagnostic record is created or exported, state purpose, included minimal fields, retention, deletion control, and that it does not affect play. `Clear diagnostic data` confirms the local-only effect. Never show save contents or dialogue in diagnostics UI. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:109:The web and installed PWA share the campaign, controls, accessibility settings, semantic UI, and local-save behaviour. Installation is an optional convenience: the title/PWA status area explains availability and has a non-modal fallback when the browser offers no install prompt. Offline status is visible but not alarming. An uncached first visit tells the player that the game cannot begin offline until its assets finish downloading; a known-good installed/cache version continues if an update check fails.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/09-contract-audit.md:30:| Settings, readable UI, accessible controls/captions/visual settings/localisation | FDN-04; FEX-06\u2013FEX-09 | Accessibility, adapter and status tests; FEX-06\u2013FEX-09 browser specs |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/09-contract-audit.md:46:| Durable-data lifecycle | Pass | FDN-05 owns immutable state/commands; FDN-06 owns snapshots, migration and quarantine; FEX-10 owns player save UI; FEX-11 owns recovery diagnostics; FEX-12 owns cache lifecycle without owning saves; QOR-04 owns rollback compatibility. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/09-contract-audit.md:59:3. The brief names account-linked state, identity, multiplayer/player safety,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md:76:bootstrap the framework before core/state/content; establish persistence and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md:119:dependencies, owned outputs, unresolved questions, gate status, and structural\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md:145:## Readiness statement\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md:150:validate, and hand off implementation instructions. This statement does not\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/decision-log.md:10:| DEC-0004 | Party/content quantities, balance, locale, audio/remapping, font/contrast / game+experience owner / before DM-04/16 | approved production choices | one bounded campaign only; no numeric/content promise | GATE-0004 |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:26:  stated verification passes.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:73:  submit commands only; persistence serializes confirmed core state only.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:75:- **Owns:** `src/core/` public command/state/event interfaces; boundary/lint\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:80:  fixture adapter can submit an action and render returned state/events without\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:81:  direct state mutation.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:91:  touch target, status, and non-colour state cues; tokens support text scaling,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:99:- **Verification:** Token build/type validation passes; sample semantic states\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:109:- **Bounded outcome:** Immutable campaign state, typed commands/results/events,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:110:  revisions, interaction IDs, deterministic RNG state, and invariant helpers\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:111:  define legal transitions without implementing later feature state machines.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:114:- **Owns:** `src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/` and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:117:  save storage, UI selection state, account profiles, or network state.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:118:- **Verification:** Unit tests show invalid commands do not mutate state,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:143:- **Acceptance evidence:** Save-state diagram, schema compatibility table,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:171:- **Bounded outcome:** The contracts state that P0 has no server resource or\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md:183:- **Acceptance evidence:** P0 authorization-exclusion statement, future\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/01-product-brief.md:23:  the stated offline single-player product; downstream contracts need human\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:9:  \"wave\": {\"number\": 1, \"state\": \"planned\", \"checkpoint_after_each_batch\": true, \"resume_from\": \"first batch whose state is not accepted; validate accepted IDs, paths, and provenance before dispatch\", \"recovery\": \"If a batch fails, retain its IDs, mark it blocked or repairable, repair only its listed output paths, validate its contracts, then resume that same batch. Do not reallocate its R IDs.\"},\nprojects/