,\"IMP-0012\"], \"deferred\": [], \"human_gates_retained\": {\"IMP-0001\":\"GATE-0001\", \"IMP-0006\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0007\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0009\":\"GATE-0005\", \"IMP-0010\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004\"}},\n   \"queued_expansion\": [\n     {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 2 after GATE-0004\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand into bounded IMP records before assigning any R IDs\"},\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\nindex 67c2b365c55b72b925528a14e78c3f710700d90e..1714aac5b27585b8994b8e4a1ac83c2f3f345af0\n--- a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\n@@ -2,6 +2,16 @@\n \n This readable companion to [`runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](runbook-authoring-manifest.json) is the persistent allocation ledger for the mock-fantasy-quest-4 authoring system. The JSON is authoritative for IDs, provenance, dependencies, output paths, counters, and recovery state. Accepted IDs are immutable: resume from the first non-accepted batch and append only at `B0007` and `R0013`.\n \n+## Dispatcher checkpoint \u2014 D0001\n+\n+D0001 expanded no chapter and allocated no B/R contracts. `SHARD-02` is the\n+first queued chapter, but `DEC-0004`/`GATE-0004` remains unresolved; `SHARD-03`\n+and `SHARD-04` retain their predecessor and gate blocks, while `SHARD-05` stays\n+held pending explicit authorisation. Every current catalogue contract\n+(`IMP-0001` through `IMP-0012`) is allocated exactly once. The dispatcher\n+therefore created [`D0002`](../authoring-runbooks/D0002.md) as the sole\n+successor, without advancing B/R counters or modifying accepted work.\n+\n ## Wave 1 \u2014 foundation contracts\n \n | Order | Batch | R contracts (maximum 7) | Dependency / parallel disposition | Checkpoint |\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Recorded D0001 as a no-allocation checkpoint because SHARD-02 is blocked by GATE-0004 and all existing IMP contracts are already allocated. Created exactly one successor dispatcher, D0002.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\"],\"test_result\":\"Passed: JSON/ledger validation for unique IMP/B/R IDs, exact one-to-one catalogue allocation, batch size, provenance, asset metadata, and acyclic dependencies; git diff whitespace checks; successor dispatcher structure validation. An initial successor check had an over-escaped regex and was immediately rerun successfully with a corrected expression.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"SHARD-02 requires unresolved DEC-0004/GATE-0004. SHARD-03 and SHARD-04 retain predecessor/gate blocks, SHARD-05 remains held, and IMP-0001 through IMP-0012 are allocated exactly once. D0001 therefore created no B/R work and recorded D0002 as its sole successor.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"dispatch ledger validation passed\\nsuccessor structure validation passed\",\"browser_log\":\"Not applicable: this changes authoring-dispatch documentation and allocation metadata only.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"This iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Expanded zero chapters and added zero IMP contracts. The first queued candidate, SHARD-02, remains ineligible until DEC-0004/GATE-0004 is explicitly resolved; this is recorded in manifest dispatch_history and the Markdown ledger.\"},{\"criterion\":\"It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Created zero B-series tasks and zero R allocations because no ready unassigned contract exists. Validation confirmed all existing batches contain at most seven R IDs.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"No B task was created in this no-allocation iteration. D0002 contains the equivalent dispatch context, output constraints, validation, checkpoint/update, collision-protection, and stop-condition sections for a future eligible wave.\"},{\"criterion\":\"If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Queued SHARD-02, SHARD-03, and SHARD-04 remain. Created exactly one successor, authoring-runbooks/D0002.md; no final audit B task was created. Focused validation confirmed D0001.md and D0002.md are the only dispatcher files.\"},{\"criterion\":\"IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Focused Node validation passed for unique IDs, allocation ownership, required provenance and asset fields, batch limits, and acyclic catalogue dependencies. D0001 made no B/R/IMP reassignment and did not advance B/R counters.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/decision-log.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\",\"runbooks/F014.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\"],\"summary\":\"Updated the authoritative and readable ledgers with the D0001 checkpoint and successor rationale; added the bounded successor dispatcher.\"},\"known_limitations\":[\"No queued chapter can be expanded until its explicit gate and dependencies are satisfied; SHARD-02 currently awaits DEC-0004/GATE-0004.\"],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: no product/browser behavior changed; this task updates planning and authoring runbooks only.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..acea536f9a1959e9736a7b1376bf0a41d8b41a02\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0002\n+sequence: 9\n+title: Resume bounded implementation-runbook authoring dispatch after gate review\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after D0001. Expand at most one\n+eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter into no more than 250 `IMP-*`\n+records, validate it, then allocate ready unassigned contracts into at most ten\n+new B-series authoring tasks with no more than seven R-series outputs each.\n+Create exactly one successor dispatcher when queued work or ready contracts\n+remain; otherwise create exactly one final audit B-series task. Exit after that\n+bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Review D0001's `dispatch_history` checkpoint and\n+only the canonical specification sections needed for a selected chapter.\n+`SHARD-02` is not eligible until `DEC-0004`/`GATE-0004` is explicitly resolved;\n+`SHARD-03` and `SHARD-04` retain their listed predecessor/gate blocks; and\n+`SHARD-05` remains held unless explicit authorisation is recorded.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- No R-series output is preassigned. Allocate R IDs only for ready, unassigned\n+  catalogue contracts discovered after the bounded chapter check.\n+- At most ten new B-series authoring runbooks, each owning no more than seven\n+  newly assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Exactly one successor dispatcher or one final audit B-series task, selected\n+  only after the queue and ready-contract check.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Preserve all accepted work and use monotonic B/R/IMP IDs. Do not infer approval\n+from a gate or from a queued state. A selected expansion must include stable\n+requirement links, ownership, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical sources; validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, provenance, and acyclic dependencies before allocation.\n+Every new B task must provide its context packet, output list, validation,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision protection, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files in this dispatcher.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the selected chapter's 250-contract limit, unique IMP/B/R IDs,\n+dependency closure and acyclicity, ownership/path collisions, allocation\n+uniqueness, provenance, and asset metadata. Confirm each B owns at most seven R\n+IDs and that no more than ten B tasks were created. Confirm the successor/final\n+audit choice against the remaining queued chapters and ready unassigned\n+contracts. Stop and report any source conflict, missing coverage, cycle,\n+collision, unresolved authority, or need to overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON and Markdown ledgers with chapter state, allocations,\n+counters, and the D0002 checkpoint only after validation. Retain reserved IDs\n+on repair; never renumber, replace, or rewrite an accepted B/R contract.\n+\n+## Collision protection\n+\n+Before creating any B, R, IMP, successor, or audit path, verify that its ID and\n+path are absent from the authoritative manifest and filesystem. On collision,\n+stop without overwriting or reusing the ID.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after at most one chapter expansion, one allocation wave, and\n+exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a recursive\n+prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\nindex 14297da79a9d792ceef58d36910f89b2a832bd84..8658e5ee05d7f524f0320681a1d98c40f8af61fb\n--- a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n@@ -7,6 +7,9 @@\n   \"expected_runbook_count\": 12,\n   \"id_counters\": {\"next_authoring_batch_id\": \"B0007\", \"next_implementation_runbook_id\": \"R0013\", \"rule\": \"Never reuse, renumber, or replace an accepted B or R ID. Append new allocations using these counters only.\"},\n   \"wave\": {\"number\": 1, \"state\": \"planned\", \"checkpoin